A||||3||AkursedX||Which Antifreeze??||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||06-14-2001||08:03 PM||||Hello all.  <P>Well my water pump just took a crap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  so I have spent all day today replacing it.  Talk about an awful job!  But anyways, since I have the system completely flushed, does anyone have any recommendations on which antifreeze to use?<P>The main reason I ask is because I was thinking of using that Dexcool stuff that GM puts in their cars nowadays.  It's supposed to last alot longer than regular antifreeze, and I was wondering if anyone had any experiences with this stuff.<P>Any feedback is appreciated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||06-14-2001||08:20 PM||||Dexcool is usually not recomended for older systems. Use our search system and you'll find a number of threads about coolant. There was a large one on Dexcool recently.<P>Any "name" brand of antifreeze in a 50/50 mix with water will work well. One important item... Use CLEAN water. The best thing to use is "deionized" or distilled water. You can get either at most grocery stores. look in the cleaning isle if you can't find it with bottled water. Using this may cost a bit but you will eliminate polutants that can shorten coolant and system life. (City water contains chlorene. Well/spring water is almost always loaded with minerals. Niether is a good thing.)||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||06-14-2001||08:34 PM||||Whoops, forgot to search in the 1st place.  But I found the thread, and I think I'll stick with the regular stuff.  and I'll think I'll take the Ogre's advice about the deionized water.  The insides of it didn't look all too great, but not too bad (93k miles)  So hopefully I can prevent further corrosion/buildup until I do my rebuild at least.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||theogre||06-14-2001||11:32 PM||||Run some flusher thru it. That should get at least some crud out. Make sure what ever flusher you use is Aluminum safe. There are still a few floating around that aren't.||||reg||1
